    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d186">

                <pb facs="0421" n="297" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg297"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.7365 W 52/27</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Italian Ambassador</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Caetani</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-06-27"><hi rendition="#italic">June 27,
                        1923</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your Excellency’s note of June 21, 1923, in which you inform me that
                    the condition quoted in my note to you of June 9, 1923, which it is proposed to
                    include in the license to be issued to the Western Union Telegraph Company,
                    authorizing the company to land a cable in the United States extending to the
                    Azores where it will connect with <pb facs="0422" n="298" xml:id="pg298"/> the
                    cable of the Italian Submarine Telegraph Cable Company,<anchor n="96"
                        xml:id="d186-f1"/> is agreeable to your Government and to the Italian
                    interests concerned in the enterprise. You state that your Government is
                    confident that practical enforcement of the condition mentioned will not be
                    undertaken without the two Governments first earnestly endeavoring to come to a
                    friendly agreement in regard to the matter.</p>
                <p>I am gratified that the proposed condition is agreeable to your Government and to
                    the Italian interests concerned, and assure you that, before taking action to
                    carry out the provisions of the condition mentioned, the Government of the
                    United States will discuss the matter with your Excellency’s Government in an
                    effort to adjust any question which may have arisen.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles E. Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d186-f1" n="96" xml:id="d186-f1-content">
                <p>The license referred to was signed by the President, Aug. 25, 1923.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
